.TH MYWORDCOUNT 3 "November 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mywordcount \- count whitespace-separated words in a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <mystrfunctions.h>
.sp
.BI "int mywordcount(const char *" str );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mywordcount
function scans the null-terminated string
.I str
and counts the number of contiguous, non-whitespace tokens ("words"),
using
.BR isspace (3)
to detect word boundaries.
.PP
If
.I str
is
.B NULL
the function returns 0.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of words found in
.IR str .
Returns 0 if
.I str
is
.B NULL
or contains no words.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <mystrfunctions.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    printf("%d\en", mywordcount("  the quick  brown fox "));  /* prints 4 */
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Written as part of the OS Assignment 01: Core C Utilities Library.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mygrep (3),
.BR myfile_stats (3)
